window.BOOKS=[
{title:'The Girl Who Carried a Kingdom',sub:'A crown was never the beginning of your magic.',color:'#6b394c',symbol:'♛',photo:0,words:['Dear Bidisha, some kingdoms are built from stone. Yours can be built from little joys, brave hopes, and a thousand beautiful things you have yet to discover.','You do not need a grand entrance to belong in your own story. Step into it exactly as you are. Let the crown be a celebration, never a condition.','On National Princess Day, here is my wish: may you feel cherished in every room you enter, and at home in every chapter you choose.']},
{title:'When Bidisha Smiles',sub:'Even the sun pauses to take notes.',color:'#a56d43',symbol:'☼',photo:2,words:['If a smile could be pressed between pages, this book would never need a lamp. It would glow softly on the shelf, waiting for the days that need a little warmth.','Bidisha, may life give you the kind of laughter that arrives without an invitation. The kind that makes an ordinary afternoon worth remembering.','And when happiness feels far away, may it find its way back gently — through a familiar voice, a favourite song, or something wonderfully small.']},
{title:'A Pocketful of Sunshine',sub:'For the golden little moments ahead.',color:'#7d803e',symbol:'✷',photo:3,words:['Here is a pocket sewn from morning light. Inside: one unhurried sunrise, a song you can never resist, and the feeling that something lovely is about to happen.','Take it with you, Bidisha, wherever your next adventure leads. Open it whenever the world forgets to be soft.','May there always be sunlight on your favourite path, and time enough to stop and enjoy it.']},
{title:'The Moon Keeps Your Name',sub:'A lullaby for the thoughts that stay awake.',color:'#484d77',symbol:'☾',photo:7,words:['Tonight, imagine the moon as a tiny librarian, carefully keeping every wish you have whispered into the dark. Nothing precious gets misplaced here.','You are allowed to rest, Bidisha. You do not have to solve every tomorrow before you close your eyes.','May the night be gentle with your thoughts. May morning arrive with a lighter heart and a fresh little beginning.']},
{title:'An Atlas of Her Dreams',sub:'No dream of yours is too far from the map.',color:'#426e6d',symbol:'✧',photo:1,words:['This atlas has no final page. Its mountains are possibilities, its rivers are curiosity, and every unmarked road is an invitation addressed to you.','Bidisha, may you find the courage to follow the things that make your eyes light up — even when the path takes its time becoming clear.','Go at your own pace. Take the scenic route. A beautiful life does not need to look like anyone else’s map.']},
{title:'The Brave Little Beginning',sub:'Every great chapter starts with one small yes.',color:'#a45a59',symbol:'❦',photo:6,words:['Once upon a time is a lovely phrase. But perhaps the most magical one is: I think I will try.','For every new beginning waiting for you, Bidisha, may there be a little courage in your pocket and someone kind cheering from the doorway.','You can begin before you know every step. Let the first one be small, let it be yours, and let that be enough for today.']},
{title:'Where the Wildflowers Bow',sub:'A garden that blooms in your own time.',color:'#54735b',symbol:'❀',photo:4,words:['In this garden, no flower is asked why it blooms later than another. The roses make room for the jasmine. The wildflowers take the long way toward the sun.','May you give yourself that same kindness, Bidisha. There is no clock on becoming, no deadline for discovering what makes you feel alive.','Grow toward the light that feels like yours. May your days be full of places where you can flourish freely.']},
{title:'The Beautiful Unwritten',sub:'For all the chapters you have yet to meet.',color:'#87627d',symbol:'∞',photo:5,words:['Somewhere ahead, there is a favourite place you have never seen. A song you have not heard. A day you will wish you could keep forever.','There is so much beautiful unwritten, Bidisha. May that thought sit beside you like an open window.','This page is not a prediction. It is a wish: that the next chapter surprises you kindly, and gives you more reasons to look forward.']},
{title:'A Spell Called Bidisha',sub:'The rarest magic never needed a wand.',color:'#71424b',symbol:'✦',photo:0,words:['The recipe is a secret, but the spell begins like this: a little wonder, a little courage, a heart allowed to dream, and a name written carefully in gold.','Bidisha. There — the page feels more magical already.','May you never feel that you must become someone else to be worthy of love, delight, or a fairytale moment. This book was made for the one and only you.']},
{title:'Letters from the Stars',sub:'Tiny reminders from a very big universe.',color:'#3e596c',symbol:'✵',photo:7,words:['Dear Bidisha, says the first star, there is room for your brightest dreams. Dear Bidisha, says the second, there is room for your quiet days, too.','The third star has only a small message: you deserve tenderness without having to earn it by being perfect.','Keep these little letters wherever you keep your hope. May they remind you that even the longest night has places where the light gets in.']},
{title:'Her Own Kind of Royal',sub:'A fairytale with no borrowed rules.',color:'#985c70',symbol:'♛',photo:4,words:['In this fairytale, the princess chooses the route. She can wear the crown or leave it on the windowsill. She can seek adventure or spend the afternoon reading.','Bidisha, may you have the freedom to make a life that feels right to you — full of your colours, your curiosities, your own beautiful choices.','Today is a little celebration of that freedom. Your story. Your pace. Your own kind of royal.']},
{title:'And She Lived Wonderfully',sub:'Not an ending. A wish for everything ahead.',color:'#76603f',symbol:'♡',photo:2,words:['Let us leave happily ever after open-ended. Let it mean good mornings, second chances, ridiculous laughter, and people who stay kind when life gets complicated.','Let it mean finding beauty in a life that is real, surprising, and entirely your own.','Happy National Princess Day, Bidisha. May you live wonderfully — in the grand adventures and in all the small, ordinary moments that turn out to be the treasure.']}
];
